          "id": "security",
          "name": "Security",
          "tagline": "Cross-cutting concerns: threat model, secrets, dependencies, audit. Apply alongside whichever other track fits the project.",
          "note": "Security touches every phase of every project. Read Common first; treat this track as the security overlay on top.",
          "phases": [
            {
              "id": "kickoff",
              "name": "1. Kick off",
              "summary": "Identify what you're protecting and from whom before any architecture decision. Threat models built after the fact are theatre.",
              "picks": [
                {
                  "concept": "Threat model (STRIDE / data flow)",
                  "why": "Map trust boundaries, data flows, and threat actors. Ninety minutes here prevents weeks of retrofitted patches. STRIDE (Spoofing, Tampering, Repudiation, Information disclosure, Denial of service, Elevation of privilege) is a good starting checklist.",
                  "example_id": "f0f72ffa5d8ca2c8",
                  "example_label": "stride-analysis-patterns",
                  "source_repo": "wshobson/agents",
                  "source_ref": "main",
                  "source_path": "plugins/security-scanning/skills/stride-analysis-patterns/SKILL.md",
