                  "skill_name": "stride-analysis-patterns",
                  "skill_dir": "plugins/security-scanning/skills/stride-analysis-patterns",
                  "composite": 0.861
                },
                {
                  "concept": "Compliance scope",
                  "why": "Identify whether PCI-DSS, HIPAA, GDPR, SOC2, or any industry-specific regulation applies. Data residency, retention, audit logging, and encryption defaults all follow from this scope.",
                  "example_id": "a7e30b6001b55ec7",
                  "example_label": "pci-compliance",
                  "source_repo": "wshobson/agents",
                  "source_ref": "main",
                  "source_path": "plugins/payment-processing/skills/pci-compliance/SKILL.md",
                  "raw_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wshobson/agents/main/plugins/payment-processing/skills/pci-compliance/SKILL.md",
                  "skill_name": "pci-compliance",
                  "skill_dir": "plugins/payment-processing/skills/pci-compliance",
                  "composite": 0.855
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "plan",
              "name": "2. Plan",
              "summary": "Authentication and data-protection design happen at planning time. These decisions are expensive to reverse mid-build.",
              "picks": [
                {
                  "concept": "Auth / authz model design",
                  "why": "Sessions vs JWT vs OAuth vs SAML; RBAC vs ABAC vs ReBAC. Decide the model and where session state lives before the first login screen. Swapping mid-project breaks everything that touched auth.",
                  "example_id": "be0b8aaefdd01b1f",
                  "example_label": "auth-implementation-patterns",
                  "source_repo": "wshobson/agents",
                  "source_ref": "main",
                  "source_path": "plugins/developer-essentials/skills/auth-implementation-patterns/SKILL.md",
